        "id": 164321,
        "name": "racingstripe",
        "username": "racingstripe",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/b9bd4f/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2016-03-06T16:26:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"jan111\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/ad7895/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> jan111:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The new heroes, especially Writhe, Akash'thriya and Benchmark. Also all the promo's. I never played a variant hero and am curious how much it changes the gameplay.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>it varies from hero to hero. &nbsp;some heroes wouldn't normally use their innate power a ton, so a variant might not have a big impact – vanilla Ra and current variant Ra games don't feel very different for me. &nbsp;other heroes use their innate almost every turn and any pertubation has enormous effect – Dad-Legacy and Kid- or PopPop-Legacy or the Scholars come to mind. &nbsp;the best variants really do almost feel like a completely new hero.</p>",
        "post_number": 32,
